---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title = "Projects" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">
  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">MY RESEARCH 🪐</div>
  </div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="Protoplanetary Disk Modelling"
    img="/HD163296.webp"
    desc="Understanding dust around a protoplanetary disk provides crucial insight into planetary
    formation processes. Multi-wavelength observations allow us to constrain the temperature,
    density, and distribution of the dust. Specifically, in the disk HD 163296, a perculiar dichotomy is 
    observed, with an outer ring being visible in the millimeter-wavelength, but invisible in the infrared.
    Here, we construct a self-consistent thick disk structure model from first principles to see if this
    dichotomy can be reproduced."
    url="#"
    badge="NEW"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Giant Impact and Moon Accretion"
    img="/lunar_formation.webp"
    desc="Using a N-body simulations combined with core-mantle differentiation models, I investigate 
    the conditions of the protolunar disk following the Giant Impact event between Proto-Earth and Theia. 
    We attempt to reconstruct the Lunar mantle's geochemistry from individual Moonlet impacts onto a target
    body to see which sets of initial compositions of moonlets can best reproduce the observed Lunar mantle."
    url="#"
    badge="In preparation"
  />

  <!-- <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5 mt-10">Projects Header</div>
  </div> -->

  <HorizontalCard
    title="Terrestrial Planet Formation"
    img="/earth_formation.webp"
    desc="We investigate various initial conditions in the protoplanetary disk such as accretion scenarios,
    oxidation gradients in the disk, and compositions of planetary building blocks to constrain 
    the evolution of terrestrial planets. Our goal is to answer these questions: 
    How did the Solar system form? What dynamical pathways led to the formation of the Earth? What was
    the geochemistry of the material that formed the Earth?"
    url="#"
    badge="Submitted"
  />
